FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: deposing-the-statutes-of-delegation.

OFF THE RECORD: This case passes powers of attorney for its local
OFF THE RECORD: offices to the delegation statute. The statute uses
OFF THE RECORD: them to map, filter, and fold without referring to
OFF THE RECORD: the local offices by name.

INCORPORATE BY REFERENCE statutes-of-delegation.

ARTICLE 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT fines IS A SCHEDULE COMPRISING 3 AND 1 AND 4 AND 1 AND 5.
    PROCLAIM THE FINDING OF applied-to-each REGARDING (A POWER OF ATTORNEY OVER THE OFFICE OF doubled) AND fines.
    PROCLAIM THE FINDING OF selected-by REGARDING (A POWER OF ATTORNEY OVER THE OFFICE OF excessive) AND fines.
    PROCLAIM THE FINDING OF folded-with REGARDING (A POWER OF ATTORNEY OVER THE OFFICE OF accumulated-with) AND fines AND 0.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT counsel IS A POWER OF ATTORNEY OVER THE OFFICE OF doubled.
    PROCLAIM THE FINDING UNDER counsel REGARDING 21.
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.

THE OFFICE OF doubled, CONCERNING amount.
    REMAND WITH amount TIMES 2.

THE OFFICE OF excessive, CONCERNING amount.
    SHOULD amount EXCEED 2, REMAND WITH SUSTAINED.
    REMAND WITH OVERRULED.

THE OFFICE OF accumulated-with, CONCERNING standing AND amount.
    REMAND WITH standing PLUS amount.
